The mandate language: RHYME, RETURN, and the repeat licence per PAIR.

§1  UNKNOWN — doctrine 28 made mechanical, not conventional
  ok    UNKNOWN is a singleton
  ok    bool(UNKNOWN) RAISES and names the doctrine   -- `None` would have been read as False by `if x:`
  ok    UNKNOWN is not False and not None
  ok    repr is readable
  ok    decided() is the branch-free reader
  ok    the requirement set is closed at five
  ok    FREE and UNDECLARED are DIFFERENT VALUES   -- 'nothing required' vs 'never asked' (doctrine 28)

§2  three statements where the language had one
  ok    statement 1 — these lines must RHYME
  ok    statement 2 — this line must RETURN verbatim
  ok    statement 3 — the return TRANSPORTS the rhyme obligation   -- L33 IS L13, so L33 answers L17 and it is not a collision
  ok    a pair the mandate declares unrhymed is FREE

    doctrine 3 inverts BY PAIR, which no song-wide switch can do
  ok    REPEAT is the REQUIREMENT at a return pair
  ok    REPEAT is a VIOLATION at a rhyme pair in the same section   -- `repeat_licence='refrain'` would license this one too
  ok    and it is a violation ACROSS the return as well   -- L37 IS L17, so slow/go must still be a rhyme
  ok    REPEAT at a free pair is UNKNOWN, not False

