§4  declaring a return does not stop mandating the rhyme
  ok    the four chorus classes span BOTH instances   [[13, 17, 33, 37], [14, 16, 34, 36], [15, 19, 35, 39], [18, 20, 38, 40]]
  ok    every cross pair is now MANDATED, so a broken one is a violation and not a collision
  ok    declaring the return ADDS mandated pairs rather than removing them   8 declared -> 24 required

§5  the licence is PER PAIR, so it cannot leak into a verse
  ok    a verse pair mandated to rhyme keeps REPEAT as a VIOLATION while the chorus return is declared   -- `repeat_licence='refrain'` licenses BOTH; this licenses one
  ok    no pair outside a return class is ever licensed
  ok    free verse pairs stay UNKNOWN rather than licensed

§6  everything the song does elsewhere is still FREE and still reportable
  ok    all ten remain FREE — the return licensed nothing about them   10 pairs

§7  refusals, and every one of them is loud
  ok    a return whose two runs are different lengths REFUSES   -- not a zip cut to the shorter run
  ok    a return class of one line REFUSES
  ok    a line that returns itself REFUSES
  ok    a return line outside the song REFUSES
  ok    a PLACED return member REFUSES BY NAME with the remedy stated — not `invalid literal for int()` from three frames down (M-142): a return class declares whole LINES identical and the identity judges read lines, so `1.head` has no judge to be handed to
  ok    ...and a member that is not a line number at all refuses in this layer's own words too
  ok    two declarations that transitively merge and DISAGREE about verbatim REFUSE   -- not a tie broken by declaration order (doctrine 66)
  ok    no mandate at all still REFUSES

    and the letters refuse rather than degrade
  ok    to_letters() REFUSES on a mandate that carries returns   -- a letter cannot say 'this line is that line come back'
  ok    the lossy projection is still available, NAMED for its loss
  ok    a return-free mandate is EXACTLY the old object

    a return declared NON-verbatim has no A-1 mark, so the notation refuses
  ok    to_notation() REFUSES a return it cannot mark
  ok    and its identity requirement is FALSE, not UNKNOWN, because it was DECLARED false
  ok    an UNDECLARED verbatim requirement propagates as UNKNOWN
  ok    and returns_check() stays SILENT about it rather than passing it

